WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.160
Welcome to the AI-enabled Research Ethics
Training Module developed by the

2
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.880
National Centre for Scientific Research,
Democritos, and co-funded by the

3
00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:14.860
European Union. Artificial intelligence is
rapidly integrating into scientific

4
00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:19.300
research methodologies, scaling across
disciplines from healthcare and social

5
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:21.920
sciences to engineering and security.

6
00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:26.780
While these computational tools offer
remarkable new analytical capabilities,

7
00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:29.940
they simultaneously introduce complex
ethical challenges.

8
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.340
that we have not had to evaluate before.

9
00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:36.000
The current frameworks utilized by
research ethics committees and

10
00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:40.360
investigators were built for human subject
trials and physical data.

11
00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:43.720
They were not designed to address
algorithmic complexities.

12
00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:48.520
This graphic illustrates our training's
core objective, to build a functional

13
00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:50.880
bridge between two distinct worlds.

14
00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:55.720
On one side, we have an accelerating
influx of emerging AI technologies.

15
00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:59.920
On the other side, we must anchor those
deployments to established ethical

16
00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:04.920
review practices. Responsible governance
cannot rely on abstract principles

17
00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:09.800
alone. To evaluate these tools properly,
we first have to understand the

18
00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:13.080
foundational architecture of how they
actually operate.
